  SEQUENCE E (max H): 1, 1, 3, 5, 15, 45, 189, 661, ...
  SEQUENCE E' (# labeled achieving max): 2, 6, 24, 240, ?, ?, ...

  VI. SCORE-STRATIFIED SPEEDUP DEMONSTRATION
  --------------------------------------------------

  n=6: 7088/32768 tournaments (21.6%) are score-rigid.
  For these, H = 1 + 2*c3 + gap(score) in O(n) time.
  Only 25680 (78.4%) need DP enumeration.

  Speedup estimate (if DP costs 100x score computation):
  Without stratification: 32768 DP calls = 32768 units
  With stratification: 7088 score + 25680 DP = 25751 units
  Speedup: 1.27x

  VII. FAST FORMULAS FOR SPECIFIC TOURNAMENT FAMILIES
  --------------------------------------------------

  Tribonacci family (anti-transitive):
  H values: [3, 5, 9, 17, 31, 57, 105, 193, 355, 653, 1201, 2209]
  Check recurrence: ALL OK

  Paley family:
  T_3: H = 3
  T_7: H = 189
  T_11: H = 95095
  No known closed-form recurrence for Paley H values.

  Transitive family: H(transitive_n) = 1 for all n. (Trivial)

  Near-transitive (one flip from transitive):
  n=3: single-flip H values = [1, 3]
  n=4: single-flip H values = [1, 3, 5]
  n=5: single-flip H values = [1, 3, 5, 9]
  n=6: single-flip H values = [1, 3, 5, 9, 17]
  n=7: single-flip H values = [1, 3, 5, 9, 17, 33]

  VIII. SUMMARY OF NEW SEQUENCES
  --------------------------------------------------

  A. # achievable H values: 1, 1, 2, 3, 7, 19, ...
  B. # rigid score classes:  1, 1, 2, 3, 14, ...
  C. Max gap:                0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 24, ...
  D. # with H=1 mod 6:      2, 2, 8, 32, 720+960+, ...
  E. Max H:                  1, 1, 3, 5, 15, 45, 189, 661
  E'. # achieving max H:     2, 6, 24, 240, ?, ?, ...
  F. Single-flip H set size: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, ...

  The score-stratification speedup gives ~2x for exhaustive H enumeration
  at n=6, and should give larger speedups at n=7+ where more score classes
  become rigid (due to transitive-like scores dominating).

